---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from '../config';
const updated = '8 August 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms of use" description="Terms governing use of this site, the limits of what is published here, and trademark and liability notices.">
<div class="wrap"><Breadcrumbs trail={[{ label: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' }]} /></div>
<section class="wrap" style="padding:1.5rem 1.25rem 0">
  <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
  <h1 style="max-width:20ch">Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="note" style="margin:1rem 0 2rem">Last updated {updated}. By using {SITE.domain} you accept these terms.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} publishes operational reference material for people selling on online marketplaces:
      fee structures, policy changes, cost arithmetic and calculators. It is published by {SITE.publisher}
      and funded by display advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Information, not advice</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here is general information. Nothing on this site is tax, legal, accounting, financial or
      investment advice, and no reader relationship creates a professional relationship of any kind. Your
      circumstances, your jurisdiction and your marketplace account terms are specific to you. Consult a
      qualified professional before acting on anything that matters.
    </p>

    <h2>Figures change, and some of them are already wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Marketplace fees, tariff rules and platform policies change on the platforms' own timetable, often
      without notice to sellers. Every rate published here carries the date it was checked and a link to
      its source for exactly that reason. A dated figure is a record of what was true on that date, not a
      guarantee of what is true today.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where published sources disagree with each other, we say so rather than picking one silently. Where
      a figure is illustrative rather than quoted from a rate card, it is labelled illustrative. Verify
      anything material against the marketplace's own documentation before you price against it, place an
      order against it, or make an inventory commitment on the strength of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Calculators</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators run in your browser and are provided as-is. They apply the arithmetic described on
      each page to the numbers you enter. They do not know your category's referral rate, your negotiated
      freight rate or your account's fee schedule, and they are not a substitute for the fee preview tools
      inside your own seller account.
    </p>

    <h2>Downloads</h2>
    <p>
      Spreadsheet templates offered here may be downloaded and used, including commercially, in your own
      operations. You may not redistribute them, resell them, or present them as your own work.
    </p>

    <h2>Our content</h2>
    <p>
      Text, tables, graphics and code on this site are the property of {SITE.publisher} unless otherwise
      credited. Quoting a short passage with attribution and a link is welcome. Republishing pages in
      whole or in substantial part, or using them to train or fine-tune a model for redistribution, is
      not permitted without written permission. Requests: <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks and independence</h2>
    <p>
      Amazon, Walmart, eBay, Etsy, TikTok, Shopify and all other marks referenced are the property of
      their respective owners and are used here for identification and commentary only. {SITE.name} is
      independent and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or otherwise associated with any
      marketplace or software vendor covered on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising and commercial disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      This site carries display advertising served by third parties. Advertisers have no visibility into
      or influence over what is published, and no advertisement constitutes an endorsement. Where a page
      mentions a product the publisher sells or has a commercial interest in, that interest is disclosed
      on the page itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not attempt to interfere with the site's operation, scrape it at a rate that degrades service for
      others, or use it for anything unlawful.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      This site is provided as-is and without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including as to
      accuracy, completeness or fitness for a particular purpose. To the fullest extent permitted by law,
      {SITE.publisher} is not liable for any loss — including lost profit, lost inventory value, fees
      incurred or business interruption — arising from reliance on anything published here. Nothing in
      these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong, tell us and send the source. Corrections are made in place with a dated
      note and logged on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. Nothing is edited silently.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Material changes to these terms are dated at the top of this page.</p>

    <p class="note">
      These terms describe how this site actually operates. They are written to be accurate rather than
      exhaustive, and they are not legal advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
